From 9b11c21291bad143c60e862e2cc4ee3ae825d91d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Luis Choque <luis.choque.castro@outlook.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 14:07:26 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] refactor(config): read R2_PUBLIC_BASE_URL and drop unused
 variables

New file URLs are built by publicFileUrl() from R2_PUBLIC_BASE_URL
(FILE_DOWNLOAD_ENDPOINT is still honoured as a fallback, so deploying
needs no env change). The stored format is unchanged: raw URL on the R2
domain.

.env.example and README no longer list variables that no code reads:
KELVINGPT_API, KELVINGPT_API_AUTHORITY, FILE_UPLOAD_ENDPOINT,
FILE_UPLOAD_TOKEN and FILE_PREVIEW_ENDPOINT. GPT_API_KEY and the R2
variables, which the code does read, are now documented.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
